d_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YehorBabenko88/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds an isolated Assignment authority substrate over the existing Grid Consul authority: distinct storage binding keys, strict runtime policy parsing, generation/session transaction fencing, bounded transactions and fail-closed native response validation. Public execute/reconcile remain unavailable pending approved domain contracts and an actual native identity provider; this does not issue Assignment grants or implement storage publication.\n\nBase: be6335a2e8cfac9483213a6a215bc29e32808b0c\nHEAD: 40e9c8dc274a2746018bc1aa08d103cd0187cecc\nTree: a67f969d95934fe39c4206021a9aabcde6b6ccab\nScope: 11 new owned files; existing frozen runtime, transport, scheduler, storage engine and UI unchanged.\n\nValidation on a fresh byte-materialized checkout: 11 unit tests, 8 real isolated three-server Consul probe groups, 8 source guard controls; 695 Grid and 674 pinned Unified raw files checked before/after. Windows Consul 1.22.2 processes were test-owned and stopped. Includes stale leader/generation rejection, same-key publication/supersession ordering, simultaneous restart persistence and loss-of-quorum denial. These are explicitly raw substrate probes, not issued Assignment or native security acceptance. Matched-cache regression and malformed success envelope failures were reproduced before fixes; focused independent review found no remaining actionable issue.\n\nAdds a dedicated Linux/Windows CI workflow; hosted results pending. Runtime policy review1 is preserved as withdrawn; review2 is an unapproved additive proposal, with existing Root identity records unchanged. Physical LS5/PC4/PC3 HA and native authority admission remain NO-GO. No merge or deployment requested.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-07T12:06:08Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T12:06:08Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_c